{"instruction": "How many MODE2/2336 sectors does a single-sector movie (2336 bytes exactly) occupy, and what is engine_size?", "input": "MOVIE_ID.BIN 20-byte record layout: LBA (u32 LE) + engine_size (u32 LE, sectors*2336)", "output": "<thinking>\nA single-sector movie (2336 bytes exactly) needs ceil(size / 2336) sectors when size > 0; engine_size is\n        stored as sectors * 2336 (the MODE2 Form 2 user-data payload per sector),\n        not the raw byte size, so partial final sectors still count as a whole sector.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM2_USER = 2336\n\ndef sectors_for_size(size: int) -> int:\n    return -(-size // FORM2_USER) if size > 0 else 0\n\ndef engine_size_for(size: int) -> int:\n    return sectors_for_size(size) * FORM2_USER\n\nsize = 2336\nassert sectors_for_size(size) == 1\nassert engine_size_for(size) == 2336\n```"}
{"instruction": "How many MODE2/2336 sectors does a sub-sector remainder movie (100 bytes) occupy, and what is engine_size?", "input": "MOVIE_ID.BIN 20-byte record layout: LBA (u32 LE) + engine_size (u32 LE, sectors*2336)", "output": "<thinking>\nA sub-sector remainder movie (100 bytes) needs ceil(size / 2336) sectors when size > 0; engine_size is\n        stored as sectors * 2336 (the MODE2 Form 2 user-data payload per sector),\n        not the raw byte size, so partial final sectors still count as a whole sector.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM2_USER = 2336\n\ndef sectors_for_size(size: int) -> int:\n    return -(-size // FORM2_USER) if size > 0 else 0\n\ndef engine_size_for(size: int) -> int:\n    return sectors_for_size(size) * FORM2_USER\n\nsize = 100\nassert sectors_for_size(size) == 1\nassert engine_size_for(size) == 2336\n```"}
{"instruction": "How many MODE2/2336 sectors does a large multi-sector movie (10 MiB) occupy, and what is engine_size?", "input": "MOVIE_ID.BIN 20-byte record layout: LBA (u32 LE) + engine_size (u32 LE, sectors*2336)", "output": "<thinking>\nA large multi-sector movie (10 MiB) needs ceil(size / 2336) sectors when size > 0; engine_size is\n        stored as sectors * 2336 (the MODE2 Form 2 user-data payload per sector),\n        not the raw byte size, so partial final sectors still count as a whole sector.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM2_USER = 2336\n\ndef sectors_for_size(size: int) -> int:\n    return -(-size // FORM2_USER) if size > 0 else 0\n\ndef engine_size_for(size: int) -> int:\n    return sectors_for_size(size) * FORM2_USER\n\nsize = 10485760\nassert sectors_for_size(size) == 4489\nassert engine_size_for(size) == 10486304\n```"}
{"instruction": "How many MODE2/2336 sectors does a multi-disc pointer table boundary (disc 2 LBA offset) occupy, and what is engine_size?", "input": "MOVIE_ID.BIN 20-byte record layout: LBA (u32 LE) + engine_size (u32 LE, sectors*2336)", "output": "<thinking>\nA multi-disc pointer table boundary (disc 2 LBA offset) needs ceil(size / 2336) sectors when size > 0; engine_size is\n        stored as sectors * 2336 (the MODE2 Form 2 user-data payload per sector),\n        not the raw byte size, so partial final sectors still count as a whole sector.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM2_USER = 2336\n\ndef sectors_for_size(size: int) -> int:\n    return -(-size // FORM2_USER) if size > 0 else 0\n\ndef engine_size_for(size: int) -> int:\n    return sectors_for_size(size) * FORM2_USER\n\nsize = 2336\nassert sectors_for_size(size) == 1\nassert engine_size_for(size) == 2336\n```"}
{"instruction": "How many MODE2/2336 sectors does a zero-length placeholder movie entry occupy, and what is engine_size?", "input": "MOVIE_ID.BIN 20-byte record layout: LBA (u32 LE) + engine_size (u32 LE, sectors*2336)", "output": "<thinking>\nA zero-length placeholder movie entry needs ceil(size / 2336) sectors when size > 0; engine_size is\n        stored as sectors * 2336 (the MODE2 Form 2 user-data payload per sector),\n        not the raw byte size, so partial final sectors still count as a whole sector.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM2_USER = 2336\n\ndef sectors_for_size(size: int) -> int:\n    return -(-size // FORM2_USER) if size > 0 else 0\n\ndef engine_size_for(size: int) -> int:\n    return sectors_for_size(size) * FORM2_USER\n\nsize = 0\nassert sectors_for_size(size) == 0\nassert engine_size_for(size) == 0\n```"}
{"instruction": "How do I detect a Form 1 sector (EDC present, user=2048) from the MODE2 subheader?", "input": "MODE2/XA subheader bytes 16-19 (mirrored at 20-23): file#, channel#, submode, coding", "output": "<thinking>\nThe submode byte's Form bit (bit 0x02) distinguishes Form1 (bit clear,\n        2048-byte user data + EDC/ECC) from Form2 (bit set, 2336-byte user data,\n        no EDC/ECC). Byte value 0x04 here has the Form bit clear -> Form1.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM_BIT = 0x02\n\ndef is_form1(submode_byte: int) -> bool:\n    return (submode_byte & FORM_BIT) == 0\n\nsubmode_byte = 0x04\nassert is_form1(submode_byte) is True\n```"}
{"instruction": "How do I detect a Form 2 sector (EDC absent, user=2336) from the MODE2 subheader?", "input": "MODE2/XA subheader bytes 16-19 (mirrored at 20-23): file#, channel#, submode, coding", "output": "<thinking>\nThe submode byte's Form bit (bit 0x02) distinguishes Form1 (bit clear,\n        2048-byte user data + EDC/ECC) from Form2 (bit set, 2336-byte user data,\n        no EDC/ECC). Byte value 0x08 here has the Form bit set -> Form2.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM_BIT = 0x08\n\ndef is_form1(submode_byte: int) -> bool:\n    return (submode_byte & FORM_BIT) == 0\n\nsubmode_byte = 0x08\nassert is_form1(submode_byte) is False\n```"}
{"instruction": "How do I detect a corrupted submode byte (invalid form) from the MODE2 subheader?", "input": "MODE2/XA subheader bytes 16-19 (mirrored at 20-23): file#, channel#, submode, coding", "output": "<thinking>\nThe submode byte's Form bit (bit 0x02) distinguishes Form1 (bit clear,\n        2048-byte user data + EDC/ECC) from Form2 (bit set, 2336-byte user data,\n        no EDC/ECC). Byte value 0x03 here is inconsistent/corrupted.\n</thinking>\n```python\nFORM_BIT = 0x02\n\ndef is_form1(submode_byte: int) -> bool:\n    return (submode_byte & FORM_BIT) == 0\n\nsubmode_byte = 0x03\nresult = is_form1(submode_byte)  # inspect manually; byte combination is non-standard\nassert result in (True, False)\n```"}
